DOLLY 7
PACKAGE voice
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST buttons@0
REQUIRES HOST microphone@0
REQUIRES HOST threads@0

# voice as speech-build links it against transcribe.cpp, with the model it
# reads: buttons and speech in the place of a keyboard, beside a terminal program.
FROM /v0.1.3/demos/speech/Dollyfile-speech-build 0f4fed533816d72bd53ca4d55525359166f194cf5ba249626dd0ca6c78e11f32
INSTALL /v0.1.3/demos/speech/Dollyfile-parakeet b1282269b272cf0786f7150935adcb63a4b250892429350ea3b6878f192ade81

EXPORTS TOOL   voice
EXPORTS FOLDER transcribe-licenses /usr/share/licenses/transcribe.cpp
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/voice.1
    voice: types what is said into the terminal program beside it, from a strip
    of buttons: transcribe.cpp with NVIDIA's Parakeet model.
    
      voice MENU [MODEL.gguf]
    
    In MENU, "[NAME] caption" begins a page of buttons and "LABEL = TEXT" is a
    button that types TEXT (\r Enter, \e Escape, \t Tab, \xHH a byte, \w a wait
    of 0.4 s). After the text, :speak listens and types what was said, :word
    types it as a search word, :paste types the clipboard and :page NAME shows
    another page. pi-phone's /etc/dolly/pi.menu is one. It needs buttons@0 and
    microphone@0; the microphone is open only while it listens, and nothing that
    is said leaves the page.
